#[summary("메서드 구문: 계좌와 거래 기록, 순위 trait, 수신자 조정 (ADR-0051, 2M-01)")]
mod ledger {
    spec fn small(x: i64) -> bool {
        -1000000 <= x && x <= 1000000
    }

    // The balance is never negative and stays small.
    #[invariant(sound)]
    struct Account { id: u64, balance: i64 }

    spec fn sound(a: &Account) -> bool {
        0 <= a.balance && a.balance <= 1000000
    }

    // The moves of an account, in order.
    struct Log { moves: Vec<i64> }

    impl Account {
        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(sound)]
        fn open(id: u64) -> Account {
            Account { id: id, balance: 0 }
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(sound)]
        fn balance(self: &Account) -> i64 {
            self.balance
        }

        // Adds `x` when the result stays in range; whether it did.
        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(sound, small)]
        fn deposit(self: &mut Account, x: i64) -> bool
            requires small(x),
        {
            if x <= 0 || self.balance + x > 1000000 {
                return false;
            }
            self.balance = self.balance + x;
            true
        }

        // Takes `x` out when the balance covers it; whether it did.
        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(sound, small)]
        fn withdraw(self: &mut Account, x: i64) -> bool
            requires small(x),
        {
            if x <= 0 || x > self.balance {
                return false;
            }
            self.balance = self.balance - x;
            true
        }
    }

    impl Log {
        #[effects(alloc)]
        fn new() -> Log {
            Log { moves: Vec::new() }
        }

        #[effects(alloc)]
        fn record(self: &mut Log, ok: bool, x: i64) -> () {
            if ok && self.moves.len() < 1000 {
                self.moves.push(x);
            }
        }

        #[effects(pure)]
        fn count(self: &Log) -> usize {
            self.moves.len()
        }

        // The moves, by value: the log is gone after.
        #[effects(pure)]
        fn close(self: Log) -> Vec<i64> {
            self.moves
        }
    }

    trait Rank {
        #[effects(pure)]
        fn rank(self: &Self) -> u64;

        #[effects(pure)]
        fn better(self: &Self, other: &Self) -> bool {
            self.rank() > other.rank()
        }
    }

    impl Rank for Account {
        #[effects(pure)]
        #[uses(sound)]
        fn rank(self: &Account) -> u64 {
            u64::try_from(self.balance / 100).unwrap()
        }
    }

    impl Rank for u64 {
        #[effects(pure)]
        fn rank(self: &u64) -> u64 {
            *self % 10
        }
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    fn top<T: Copy + Rank>(xs: &[T]) -> u64 {
        let mut best: u64 = 0;
        for i in 0..xs.len()
            invariant i <= xs.len(),
        {
            let r: u64 = xs[i].rank();
            if r > best {
                best = r;
            }
        }
        best
    }

    spec fn bit(r: i64) -> bool {
        0 <= r && r <= 1
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(bit)]
    fn flag(b: bool) -> (r: i64)
        ensures bit(r),
    {
        if b { 1 } else { 0 }
    }

    #[effects(alloc, io)]
    #[uses(sound, small, bit)]
    fn main() -> () {
        let mut a: Account = Account::open(1);
        let mut b: Account = Account::open(2);
        let mut log: Log = Log::new();
        let ok: bool = a.deposit(500);
        log.record(ok, 500);
        let ok2: bool = a.withdraw(800);
        log.record(ok2, -800);
        let ok3: bool = a.withdraw(120);
        log.record(ok3, -120);
        print_i64(flag(ok) + flag(ok2) * 10 + flag(ok3) * 100);
        print_i64(flag(b.deposit(999999)));
        print_i64(flag(b.deposit(2)));
        print_i64(a.balance());
        print_i64(b.balance());
        print_u64(a.rank());
        print_i64(flag(b.better(&a)));
        print_i64(flag(a.better(&b)));
        let digits: [u64; 4] = [12, 7, 45, 31];
        print_u64(top::<u64>(&digits));
        print_u64(digits[1].rank());
        print_u64(u64::try_from(log.count()).unwrap());
        print_u64(b.id);
        let moves: Vec<i64> = log.close();
        for i in 0..moves.len()
            invariant i <= moves.len(),
        {
            print_i64(moves[i]);
        }
    }
}
